{"name":"Golden Glitter","hex":"#fbe573","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"golden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of, or relating to, gold.","Having a color or other richness suggestive of gold."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["(Can we verify this sense?) brassy drummer, brassy chub, etc. (Kyphosus vaigiensis), a fish found in southeast Asia.","Ellipsis of golden retriever."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/golden"},{"term":"glitter","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A bright, sparkling light; shininess or brilliance.","A shiny, decorative adornment, sometimes sprinkled on glue to make simple artwork."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To sparkle with light; to shine with a brilliant and broken light or showy luster; to gleam.","To be showy, specious, or striking, and hence attractive."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glitter"}],"entries":[{"title":"Glitter","blocks":[{"text":"Glitter is an assortment of flat, small, reflective particles that are precision cut and come in a variety of shapes, sizes, and colors. Glitter particles resemble confetti, sparkles and sequins, but are somewhat smaller."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Glitter_close_up.jpg/330px-Glitter_close_up.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glitter","wikidata":"Q1531522"},{"title":"Gold (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Gold, also called golden, is a color tone resembling the chemical element gold."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg/330px-GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_(color)","wikidata":"Q208045"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Mica_3157.jpg/500px-Mica_3157.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=pars